senses.gloss:
उभय ubhá-ya, a. (ī) sg. & pl. both;
 -kāma, 🞄a. desirous of both;
 -guṇa, a. having both qualities 🞄-cakravartin, a. ruling both worlds.

उभयतस् ubhayá-tas, ad. from or on both 🞄sides, of, (ac. or g.);
 in both cases;
 (ḥ) -sasya, 🞄a. bearing crops at both seasons;
 -tas-tīkṣṇa, 🞄a. sharp at both ends;
 -to-dant, a. having 🞄two rows of teeth;
 (á) to-mukha, having 🞄a spout on both sides (vessel).

उभयत्र ubhayá-tra, ad. in both places;
 in 🞄both cases;
 -thā, ad. in both ways or cases.

उभयप्राप्ति ubhaya-prāpti, a. validity in both 🞄cases (gr.);
 a. valid in both cases;
 -vetana, 🞄a. receiving wages from both, serving two 🞄masters;
 -snātaka, a. having bathed after both 🞄(i. e. his apprenticeship and his vow of chasitity).
